1
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:11,620
Senpai, a package has arrived for you.

2
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:13,180
What? Is it food?

3
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:16,080
A relative from Shibamata brought it over.

4
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:18,240
The tempura shop owner

5
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:21,020
It was really heavy, though.

6
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:23,120
It's a mold.

7
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:25,831
Now that I think about it, back in the day,

8
00:00:25,881 --> 00:00:29,460
I remember leaving it with someone, since it
would get thrown out if I kept it at my place.

9
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:31,680
What is it? A cookie cutter?

10
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:33,540
It's not that classy of a thing.

11
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:37,400
You pack this mud-like clay
inside and take a mold of it.

12
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:39,800
You bought things like this?

13
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:41,280
It was street vending.

14
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:47,060
There was this kind of come-on sales setup that set up
shop targeting elementary schoolers on their way home.

15
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:50,580
Magic tricks, or those
"sound-making" potions you dip a cup into,

16
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:53,380
they were selling stuff kids would love.

17
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:57,580
This mold, clay, and gold powder
were a set for about 30 yen, I think.

18
00:00:58,220 --> 00:00:59,200
Gold powder?

19
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:01,820
You paint it onto the clay
you made the mold with.

20
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:03,000
And then what do you do with it?

21
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:06,540
You show it to the mold shop uncle
and get a points ticket for it.

22
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:09,780
The bigger one gets a prize.

23
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:13,100
Looking back, he was a shady old man.

24
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:15,000
We do judge them, though.

25
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,260
Mister, I finished mine.

26
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:17,440
Who's next? Who's next?

27
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:20,500
Gold alone won't cut it.

28
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:21,980
200 points.

29
00:01:21,980 --> 00:01:26,200
You should use more
red-silver and blue-silver.

30
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:27,680
Mister, I finished mine too.

31
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:28,660
Wow, amazing!

32
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:30,200
This one gets 5,000 points.

33
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:30,840
Really?

34
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:34,160
Using five colors of lapis lazuli, nice.

35
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:36,720
In the end, it's not so much
about the quality of the work...

36
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:39,500
That's how the rating gets decided.

37
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:41,420
A pretty harsh rating

38
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:43,880
But when you give up and try to head home,

39
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:44,980
you suddenly get a good score.

40
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:46,460
This one's worth 1,000 points.

41
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:50,420
They really are watching
how hard you're trying.

42
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:51,200
Naive.

43
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:53,300
It's bait so they won't go home.

44
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:56,700
Once the points pile up,
they'll work hard to collect them, right?

45
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:57,700
Yes!

46
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:59,220
It's 7,000 points, exchange it.

47
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:02,440
Kid, it'd be a waste to exchange it now.

48
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:04,060
With just 3,000 more points,

49
00:02:04,060 --> 00:02:05,720
you'll get a mold this big.

50
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:07,120
Yeah, that makes sense.

51
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:09,600
Alright, let's try harder!

52
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:10,720
Clay, please.

53
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:12,420
Good luck!

54
00:02:12,420 --> 00:02:15,780
When you go the next day,
the mold shop's already gone.

55
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:17,660
That's quite a twist, isn't it?

56
00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:18,600
Sneaky!

57
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:22,760
Most of them vanished around the fourth day,
when the points had piled up.

58
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:26,300
You throw away the point tickets and wait until they've forgotten,
then come back.

59
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:29,660
Kids are dumb,
so they fall for the same trick again.

60
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:30,240
I see.

61
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:33,860
I once kept my points
for ages and sued them.

62
00:02:34,420 --> 00:02:34,780
Yeah.

63
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:36,980
This case involves a
different mold shop, right?

64
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:39,320
He's not like that old man, is he?

65
00:02:39,320 --> 00:02:40,480
See?

66
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:42,780
I don't really remember well, but

67
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:45,020
that man was a bad guy.

68
00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:47,540
Relax, he's not like that old man.

69
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:48,960
Good.

70
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:52,960
He puts you at ease, then by the
fourth day he's gone without a trace.

71
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:56,300
This kind of sounds like
modern fraud schemes.

72
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:59,960
I've even followed Kataya
to find out who he really is.

73
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:01,560
That's just like you, Ryo-chan.

74
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:03,940
Come on, kid, hurry home.

75
00:03:03,940 --> 00:03:07,480
No way, he'll probably vanish around tomorrow,
so we need to track down his house.

76
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:09,620
First, I'll give you 100 yen.

77
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:10,820
Really? For real?

78
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:14,220
Wow, yay! Easy money!

79
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:15,860
It's a button.

80
00:03:16,660 --> 00:03:19,400
When I turned around,
the old man was already gone.

81
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:24,080
When it comes to vanishing,
it was pure artistry.

82
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:27,160
I mean, today's story isn't about this.

83
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:29,360
You can't eat molds, can you?

84
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:33,740
Well, I'll just drink some
tea and try to ease my hunger.

85
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:36,000
Wh-what the heck is this?!

86
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:44,140
When you watch TV, keep the room
bright and sit back a bit, okay?

87
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:57,260
Anyone without money, come to me.

88
00:03:58,180 --> 00:04:02,020
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

89
00:04:02,020 --> 00:04:15,940
Look at the blue sky and white clouds.
Somehow, it'll all work out eventually.

90
00:04:28,940 --> 00:04:32,900
Anyone without a job, come to me.

91
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:37,520
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

92
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:51,280
Look at the burning sky.
Somehow, it'll all work out eventually.

93
00:04:53,400 --> 00:05:00,580
Got it? Got it, got it. Once you understand,
collect your points and follow me.

94
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:16,160
Magic kettle

95
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:20,580
What the heck is this?!

96
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:23,640
What's wrong, Ryo-chan?

97
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:25,500
Well, the kettle...

98
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:28,320
There's a hole in it.

99
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:30,700
Damn it, I can't even drink tea like this.

100
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:34,980
So that's why Ryo-san is in such a bad mood?

101
00:05:34,980 --> 00:05:35,680
Yeah.

102
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:40,280
It's not like I wanted tea or anything.

103
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:43,680
I was just trying to drink some tea
to distract myself from being hungry.

104
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:46,280
Is this month's salary already gone?

105
00:05:47,140 --> 00:05:49,580
This is all that's left.

106
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:52,580
Can't even buy cheap sweets with 5 yen?

107
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:55,460
Maybe I could buy some bread crusts,
at least.

108
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:58,180
Bread crusts won't fill me up.

109
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:02,140
If Ryo-san were a rat, we'd be full.

110
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:04,220
Don't say such nonsense.

111
00:06:04,740 --> 00:06:05,560
Sorry.

112
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:09,072
Heh heh, in this state I'm in,

113
00:06:09,122 --> 00:06:12,060
I might as well really become a rat.

114
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:13,720
I'm completely skint!

115
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:20,480
Whoa! What's going on here?!

116
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:23,400
But you just said it'd
be better to be a rat!

117
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:28,960
Kōme-chan!

118
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:33,360
Hanayama Kōme.
A high school girl who lives in heaven.

119
00:06:33,540 --> 00:06:36,720
Since she lives in heaven,
she can naturally use magic too.

120
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:40,820
Her grandfather works for
the police in heaven, but

121
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:43,020
Well, never mind about her.

122
00:06:43,020 --> 00:06:44,340
What did you say, you little...?

123
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:49,880
Hello everyone, long time no see.

124
00:06:49,880 --> 00:06:52,600
Really, you were doing well, Kōme-chan.

125
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:54,400
Since the spring special
the year before last, right?

126
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:55,440
Hello.

127
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:59,100
Hey, skip the greetings and
hurry up and change back to normal.

128
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:01,840
I'm sorry, Ryo-san.

129
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:03,720
Just normal, zip zip!

130
00:07:06,440 --> 00:07:09,060
You still haven't changed back to normal,
have you?

131
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:10,700
Sorry.

132
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:14,160
Thanks for coming by so often.

133
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:16,700
So this is your first time meeting Maria,
isn't it?

134
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:20,340
Nice to meet you, I'm Maria.
Pleased to meet you.

135
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:21,880
The pleasure's all mine.

136
00:07:22,460 --> 00:07:25,120
She's gorgeous!
Is she by any chance Ryo-san's girlfriend?

137
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:27,540
Don't be ridiculous, that's impossible.

138
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:31,240
Someone's phone is ringing.

139
00:07:31,900 --> 00:07:34,420
Oh, it's mine.

140
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:37,740
So even high school girls
in heaven have cell phones.

141
00:07:38,180 --> 00:07:40,140
It's from Grandpa, as I expected.

142
00:07:40,140 --> 00:07:44,440
He keeps nagging me to check in regularly
whenever I go down to the human world.

143
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:46,100
What an overprotective old man.

144
00:07:46,540 --> 00:07:46,900
Yes.

145
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:50,740
Yeah, I'm at Ryo-san's place right now.

146
00:07:51,540 --> 00:07:55,380
Well, there's this really gorgeous guardian,
Maria-san.

147
00:07:55,380 --> 00:07:56,900
What the heck?

148
00:07:57,620 --> 00:07:59,980
I thought I heard something just now.

149
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:02,540
Grandpa.

150
00:08:02,540 --> 00:08:03,840
Damn old geezer.

151
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:06,800
Where is she?
The really beautiful Maria-san?

152
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:09,700
So you're Maria-san?

153
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:10,400
Yes.

154
00:08:10,820 --> 00:08:15,380
I'm Rika Hanayama, Chief of the Lower World Security Division of the Heaven Police.
Nice to meet you.

155
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,020
Wow, she really is a beautiful lady.

156
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:20,220
Are you free right now?

157
00:08:20,220 --> 00:08:22,260
Would you like to come over
to my place for some tea?

158
00:08:22,260 --> 00:08:24,000
It's right upstairs from here.

159
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,860
Look at him hitting on women right here.

160
00:08:25,860 --> 00:08:28,720
I wonder if she doesn't
realize Maria-chan is a man.

161
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:30,100
Probably.

162
00:08:30,100 --> 00:08:30,840
Pretty good, right?

163
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:37,720
If we're lucky, we might get to
stuff ourselves with heavenly food.

164
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:39,500
A little bit wouldn't hurt, right?

165
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:40,400
Ryo-sama.

166
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:42,880
Maria, you should go along with him.

167
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:46,940
You're quite the understanding one,
aren't you.

168
00:08:46,940 --> 00:08:48,960
In exchange, I'm coming along too.

169
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:50,700
Ryo-sama.

170
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:53,960
You're not needed.
Maria alone is enough, right?

171
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:57,580
If I'm not with her,
Maria won't go to your place.

172
00:08:58,180 --> 00:09:01,520
I guess it can't be helped.
I'll take you along too.

173
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:05,760
So how exactly do we get to heaven?

174
00:09:06,180 --> 00:09:07,140
Just wait a moment.

175
00:09:07,140 --> 00:09:09,000
Maikka, maikka.

176
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,220
Hoi hoi.

177
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:14,800
Well, see you, Kome-chan.

178
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:17,300
Make something up for the Chief, will you?

179
00:09:17,860 --> 00:09:19,480
Keep a proper watch, you hear?

180
00:09:27,780 --> 00:09:29,120
They really went and left.

181
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:42,440
Is this heaven?

182
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:45,840
Aside from the cars flying, it's not much
different from the earthly world, is it.

183
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:47,660
That's not true.

184
00:09:47,660 --> 00:09:50,580
Heaven has all sorts of tourist attractions,
you know.

185
00:09:50,580 --> 00:09:54,200
Look, that's the famous Heaven Tower.

186
00:09:56,340 --> 00:09:58,480
It looks like a really cheap knockoff,
doesn't it.

187
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:01,380
And over there is the famous Heaven Castle.

188
00:10:01,380 --> 00:10:03,160
It's getting more and more suspicious.

189
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:04,900
Heaven Rat Land.

190
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:06,580
Hey, hey, is this really okay?
Are you sure about this?

191
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:08,460
Heaven Rainbow Bridge.

192
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:10,180
Heaven TV

193
00:10:10,180 --> 00:10:13,660
It's all just copies of buildings from Earth,
isn't it?

194
00:10:13,660 --> 00:10:16,840
No, the people on Earth copied it.

195
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:18,500
How would they copy it?

196
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:20,740
Maybe you can see Earth from heaven,

197
00:10:20,740 --> 00:10:22,900
but you can't see heaven from Earth.

198
00:10:22,900 --> 00:10:23,720
No way, you're lying.

199
00:10:24,380 --> 00:10:26,740
Stop nitpicking over little details.

200
00:10:26,740 --> 00:10:27,660
Ryo-san

201
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:30,160
He's a violent old geezer.

202
00:10:31,740 --> 00:10:32,700
That's what he said.

203
00:10:34,620 --> 00:10:36,380
Is this your house?

204
00:10:36,460 --> 00:10:37,240
That's right.

205
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:40,200
It looks like an old detached
Tokyo Metropolitan Housing unit.

206
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:41,740
Mind your own business.

207
00:10:44,940 --> 00:10:47,520
Inside, it's just like the old downtown too!

208
00:10:48,340 --> 00:10:51,240
Even in heaven,
life is the same as in the outside world.

209
00:10:52,420 --> 00:10:53,860
I'll make some tea now.

210
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:56,980
Since we're here, I'd like to eat
some heavenly food or something.

211
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:58,380
Sure, that's fine.

212
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,040
What a shameless fellow.

213
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:03,480
I don't want to hear that from you.

214
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:07,120
That's right.

215
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:10,340
Would you take a look at the
ink painting I made, Maria?

216
00:11:10,340 --> 00:11:10,920
Yes.

217
00:11:12,340 --> 00:11:13,240
Well, what do you think?

218
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:14,760
Wow, how beautiful.

219
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:17,260
I didn't know Grandpa
had this kind of hobby.

220
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,240
Shoo, shoo.

221
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:22,040
Not that you'd understand
anything about painting anyway.

222
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:24,860
I'll kill some time until the meal is ready.

223
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,560
Got it.

224
00:11:28,780 --> 00:11:32,600
It's exactly like the old downtown.

225
00:11:36,760 --> 00:11:39,740
It reminds me of a friend's
house I used to visit long ago.

226
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:48,320
Wait, it'll be ready soon.

227
00:11:51,420 --> 00:11:52,180
I'm bored.

228
00:11:57,480 --> 00:11:59,800
Why is there a kettle here?

229
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:01,620
I have no idea.

230
00:12:01,620 --> 00:12:03,900
We have our own kettle, after all.

231
00:12:03,900 --> 00:12:06,160
I wonder if Grandpa left it here.

232
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:07,160
That old man...

233
00:12:07,160 --> 00:12:07,900
Right.

234
00:12:07,900 --> 00:12:10,040
The police box's kettle was broken.

235
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:11,380
Can we take it?

236
00:12:12,020 --> 00:12:13,460
I don't think it matters.

237
00:12:13,460 --> 00:12:15,040
Then I'll take it.

238
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:15,820
Ryo-san.

239
00:12:15,820 --> 00:12:19,040
Go tell Grandpa to get the table set.

240
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:19,900
Got it.

241
00:12:21,260 --> 00:12:24,740
Maria-san, you're beautiful.

242
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:27,420
I've never seen such a beauty.

243
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:31,580
I've got the beauty's
heart in the palm of my hand!

244
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:35,440
Grandpa, the meal's ready.
Hurry up and set the table!

245
00:12:35,820 --> 00:12:38,220
At this rate, our date's going to be ruined!

246
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:41,280
Maria, it's a UFO!

247
00:12:41,280 --> 00:12:41,560
What?

248
00:12:42,880 --> 00:12:44,220
W-where?

249
00:12:44,220 --> 00:12:45,400
Aaaaah!

250
00:12:45,400 --> 00:12:46,620
Aaaaah!

251
00:12:48,940 --> 00:12:50,380
Where's this "UFO" you're talking about?

252
00:12:51,620 --> 00:12:53,020
What's wrong, Ryo-chan?

253
00:12:53,020 --> 00:12:57,500
Ngh, I've been had.
That old geezer's doing, I bet.

254
00:12:57,500 --> 00:12:59,900
Damn it, I missed out on the feast!

255
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:04,720
Damn it, the only souvenir
from heaven is this kettle?

256
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:06,980
Oh well, guess I'll make some tea with this.

257
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:12,220
Ow

258
00:13:12,220 --> 00:13:13,840
What? What is this? What?

259
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:15,500
Turn off the fire! Turn off the fire!

260
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:17,520
Still not...? Still not?

261
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:18,640
Hurry up, hurry up!

262
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:19,400
It's hot, hot, hot!

263
00:13:20,060 --> 00:13:21,720
I'm going to get burned,
I'm going to get burned!

264
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:23,920
Saved!

265
00:13:23,920 --> 00:13:27,300
Who the hell are you?

266
00:13:27,300 --> 00:13:29,780
Yes, I'm the magic kettle, desu.

267
00:13:29,780 --> 00:13:31,880
Magic kettle?

268
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:34,800
Yes, I am the magic kettle, desu!

269
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:41,080
If you're calling yourself a magic kettle,
you should be able to use magic, right?

270
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:43,300
So, what can you do?

271
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:46,380
My specialty is making money grow.

272
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:48,120
Really?

273
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:50,200
If you doubt me, I'll show you.

274
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:52,420
Put some money inside me and see.

275
00:13:52,420 --> 00:13:53,200
A-all right.

276
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:56,060
Let's see, five yen

277
00:13:56,060 --> 00:13:57,560
This is all I've got on me.

278
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:59,980
Well, it's just a test, after all.

279
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:01,280
Okay.

280
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:07,360
Grow, grow, money, grow!

281
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:09,060
Okay, okay.

282
00:14:09,060 --> 00:14:11,180
How wonderful!

283
00:14:11,900 --> 00:14:14,560
Hey, what happens if I put this in again?

284
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:16,540
I'll make it grow again, just watch.

285
00:14:16,540 --> 00:14:18,220
Alright, go on and try it.

286
00:14:19,340 --> 00:14:20,000
Ten.

287
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:23,920
Grow, grow, money, grow!

288
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:25,060
Yes, yes.

289
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:28,160
Grow, grow!

290
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:30,960
Grow, grow!

291
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:33,340
Woohoo!

292
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:38,220
Even after all that, it's still only 80 yen?

293
00:14:38,220 --> 00:14:39,180
What's the matter?

294
00:14:39,700 --> 00:14:42,500
Can't you make it a hundred
times bigger all at once?

295
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:44,900
I can only manage double, that's my limit.

296
00:14:44,900 --> 00:14:46,960
The starting amount is just too small.

297
00:14:47,660 --> 00:14:48,640
Then!

298
00:14:48,860 --> 00:14:50,720
A ten-thousand yen bill?

299
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:55,640
No way! The Chief told us
not to lend money to Ryo-chan.

300
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:56,927
Just one minute

301
00:14:56,977 --> 00:14:59,820
No, thirty seconds is fine.
I'll pay you back right away.

302
00:15:00,340 --> 00:15:04,020
But I don't carry any cash at all.

303
00:15:04,020 --> 00:15:04,480
What?

304
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:07,660
Lately you can use cards at any shop.

305
00:15:07,660 --> 00:15:10,020
There's no need to carry it around.

306
00:15:10,020 --> 00:15:11,360
For crying out loud.

307
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:17,140
If I carry too much,
Ryo-chan will just borrow it from me.

308
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:19,900
Damn, this is why rich
people are so annoying.

309
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:23,900
Nakagawa, you carry cash on you, right?

310
00:15:23,900 --> 00:15:24,560
Yeah.

311
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:26,820
I'll pay you back in thirty seconds,
I promise.

312
00:15:26,820 --> 00:15:29,580
So could you just hand over
one ten-thousand-yen bill?

313
00:15:30,140 --> 00:15:30,540
But...

314
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,940
Don't you trust me?

315
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:34,460
Fine, I'll lend it to you.

316
00:15:34,460 --> 00:15:35,480
Thanks a lot.

317
00:15:36,320 --> 00:15:39,060
Just pay me back right away, I mean it!

318
00:15:39,060 --> 00:15:41,320
I don't have much pocket money either,
you know.

319
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:43,020
Hurry, hurry!

320
00:15:43,020 --> 00:15:45,080
Huh?

321
00:15:45,740 --> 00:15:46,540
What's wrong?

322
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:49,260
What do I do? I think I dropped my wallet.

323
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:50,180
What?

324
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:53,160
It must have been during
the patrol just now.

325
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:55,040
My pocket money!

326
00:15:56,820 --> 00:15:58,080
Don't you drop your wallet again!

327
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:02,820
Damn it! And we had a magic kettle!

328
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:05,040
What a waste of a treasure!

329
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:08,680
Hey! Can't that thing do any other magic?

330
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:12,060
W-well, the only other thing it can do is...

331
00:16:12,060 --> 00:16:15,280
turn pebbles into diamonds, that's all.

332
00:16:15,740 --> 00:16:17,260
Pebbles into diamonds?

333
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:21,140
Why didn't you say that first!

334
00:16:21,700 --> 00:16:24,820
Alright, wait there!
I'll go get you a stone right now!

335
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:28,020
What's wrong?

336
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:32,660
Chief Ohara.

337
00:16:33,260 --> 00:16:35,845
I heard from Terai on
the phone just now, but

338
00:16:35,895 --> 00:16:37,360
the kettle broke, I hear.

339
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:39,460
Yeah, it got a hole in it.

340
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:41,800
I'll swap it out on my way to the station.

341
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:43,360
Is there one in the back?

342
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:44,380
I'll

343
00:16:44,380 --> 00:16:45,540
Yeah, go ahead.

344
00:16:47,660 --> 00:16:48,480
This one

345
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:53,880
I'll bring a new one right away.

346
00:16:57,500 --> 00:16:59,860
Engine, tires, tires, tires

347
00:17:00,580 --> 00:17:04,040
Senpai, just now Chief Ohara

348
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:04,820
Later, later

349
00:17:04,820 --> 00:17:08,460
Do you guys know where that kettle was?

350
00:17:08,460 --> 00:17:11,320
Chief Ohara took it.

351
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:11,880
What?

352
00:17:12,480 --> 00:17:14,340
He said he'd swap it for a new one.

353
00:17:14,940 --> 00:17:15,660
What the hell?

354
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:18,240
He went and did it on his own.

355
00:17:20,140 --> 00:17:22,700
You must've been really
attached to that kettle

356
00:17:23,100 --> 00:17:24,440
We did a bad thing.

357
00:17:26,820 --> 00:17:30,520
What do you think you're doing, Chief!
That's no ordinary kettle!

358
00:17:31,220 --> 00:17:31,980
Give it back!

359
00:17:32,860 --> 00:17:33,560
No!

360
00:17:33,620 --> 00:17:34,620
Grrr!

361
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:36,820
The kettle!

362
00:17:37,340 --> 00:17:39,340
Hey, where's the kettle?

363
00:17:39,360 --> 00:17:40,220
K-kettle?

364
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:42,440
Where's my kettle?

365
00:17:42,540 --> 00:17:43,260
My kettle!

366
00:17:44,660 --> 00:17:45,540
Kettle!

367
00:17:45,620 --> 00:17:46,220
Whoa!

368
00:17:46,780 --> 00:17:47,420
Look!

369
00:17:47,740 --> 00:17:48,660
Where is it?

370
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:50,540
The kettle is - !

371
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:52,180
What?!

372
00:17:52,340 --> 00:17:54,280
The kettle, the kettle…

373
00:17:54,880 --> 00:17:56,360
The kettle's right over there…

374
00:17:56,820 --> 00:17:59,300
Found it! Kettle-chan!

375
00:18:04,940 --> 00:18:05,740
Hey, hey!

376
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:07,440
Ryotsu, Kankichi, you!

377
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:09,780
Are you okay, kettle?

378
00:18:10,740 --> 00:18:13,840
Look closer, it's a totally different shape!

379
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:15,880
Damn it! Kettle!

380
00:18:17,060 --> 00:18:18,480
What was that all about?

381
00:18:18,480 --> 00:18:20,720
He's finally lost it.

382
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:23,900
Kettle! Where's the kettle?!

383
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:27,260
Chief!

384
00:18:29,240 --> 00:18:31,300
Where's the kettle? Where's the kettle?

385
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:32,920
Ah, here it is.

386
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:35,360
It's the kettle!

387
00:18:35,360 --> 00:18:36,140
Hm

388
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:38,780
I didn't expect you to be this happy.

389
00:18:39,260 --> 00:18:41,760
Swapping it for a new one was worth it.

390
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:43,460
A new one?

391
00:18:45,740 --> 00:18:46,840
What's wrong, Ryotsu?

392
00:18:47,020 --> 00:18:50,280
This isn't it!
It's the one you took from the police box!

393
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:52,680
Well, I left it in the supply room.

394
00:18:52,680 --> 00:18:55,040
The supply room, got it! The kettle!

395
00:18:56,820 --> 00:18:59,680
That kettle, kettle, kettle...

396
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:11,580
Where are you? Answer me, kettle! Where the hell are you,
kettle? Where did you go, kettle?

397
00:19:12,580 --> 00:19:14,100
Kettle!

398
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:20,060
Hey! Don't you have any other kettles?

399
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:23,740
I-I think the rugby club guys took it.

400
00:19:23,740 --> 00:19:25,380
Right, the rugby club it is!

401
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:31,920
Alright!
I'm gonna pour the magic water on it now!

402
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:40,380
It's really magic water!

403
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:42,480
Hey! That's my kettle!

404
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:44,480
Kettle!

405
00:19:44,480 --> 00:19:46,680
Hey! Don't take it without asking!

406
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:48,360
Draw!

407
00:19:48,740 --> 00:19:52,200
I'm not letting them take it!

408
00:19:58,200 --> 00:19:59,020
Get out of the way!

409
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:00,500
Cash!

410
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:10,960
Are you okay, Yakan?

411
00:20:11,440 --> 00:20:14,440
Gyo-san,
I drank some water and now I feel sick.

412
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:16,760
Alright, alright,
then I'll make you eat a stone.

413
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:21,240
What?

414
00:20:21,900 --> 00:20:24,260
Turn it into a diamond, Logan.

415
00:20:24,260 --> 00:20:25,480
Right. That's right.

416
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:26,260
Alright, here we go.

417
00:20:26,260 --> 00:20:28,900
Rolly-polly, roasted, shiny-shiny.

418
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:29,320
There.

419
00:20:31,760 --> 00:20:32,640
Yay!

420
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:34,940
This is going to make us a fortune!

421
00:20:34,940 --> 00:20:37,140
But first, let's eat.

422
00:20:39,360 --> 00:20:41,140
It was really delicious.

423
00:20:41,580 --> 00:20:44,280
Kōme-san, you're such a good cook.

424
00:20:45,140 --> 00:20:46,600
I'm a little confident about it.

425
00:20:47,060 --> 00:20:52,080
Ryo-sama left so suddenly without
even eating this delicious food.

426
00:20:52,460 --> 00:20:52,900
*Gasp*

427
00:20:53,840 --> 00:20:56,660
He said he suddenly remembered
some urgent business.

428
00:20:56,660 --> 00:20:58,940
He's a busy guy, after all.

429
00:20:59,580 --> 00:21:02,420
I should be taking my leave soon, too.

430
00:21:02,420 --> 00:21:05,200
Can't you stay a little longer?

431
00:21:05,780 --> 00:21:07,420
But I have work to do.

432
00:21:07,420 --> 00:21:10,880
That's right, before you go,
let me show you something rare.

433
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:13,760
If I give her a diamond
with that night view,

434
00:21:13,760 --> 00:21:16,020
I'll win Maria-chan's heart, too!

435
00:21:16,600 --> 00:21:18,040
I got it the other day.

436
00:21:18,660 --> 00:21:19,200
Here.

437
00:21:22,780 --> 00:21:23,140
Ah

438
00:21:23,700 --> 00:21:24,640
What is it?

439
00:21:24,820 --> 00:21:26,560
Sorry, sorry.

440
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:28,360
What? Grandpa?

441
00:21:28,360 --> 00:21:30,640
Sorry, the kettle that was here

442
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:32,040
I gave it to Ryo-san.

443
00:21:32,440 --> 00:21:33,500
What did you say?!

444
00:21:36,060 --> 00:21:39,580
I'm sorry,
I didn't know it was a magic kettle.

445
00:21:39,580 --> 00:21:42,300
Damn it, you're always getting in my way.

446
00:21:44,440 --> 00:21:45,600
It's over there, then.

447
00:21:46,600 --> 00:22:16,560
Mmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm...

448
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:21,120
If I get tired, please let me rest.

449
00:22:21,980 --> 00:22:22,860
Please, go ahead.

450
00:22:34,500 --> 00:22:37,080
Something feels strange in my head...

451
00:22:40,360 --> 00:22:41,460
Could this be...

452
00:22:41,460 --> 00:22:43,020
No, that can't be right.

453
00:22:43,020 --> 00:22:45,020
I just heard something,

454
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:47,420
that he's a man.

455
00:22:48,040 --> 00:22:49,800
M-m-m-m-man!

456
00:22:50,480 --> 00:22:52,640
Ahahaha!

457
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:54,180
Ahahaha!

458
00:22:54,740 --> 00:23:06,600
Ahahaha!

459
00:23:06,600 --> 00:23:08,380
That'll be 1,275 yen.

460
00:23:08,380 --> 00:23:09,440
That's cheap.

461
00:23:09,440 --> 00:23:11,580
I'll come back and eat here often.

462
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:13,980
Then I'll pay with a diamond.

463
00:23:13,980 --> 00:23:15,120
And so,

464
00:23:17,320 --> 00:23:19,180
Call a gemologist for me.

465
00:23:19,180 --> 00:23:22,480
They should buy it for a hefty price.

466
00:23:23,400 --> 00:23:24,280
This one?

467
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:27,320
Are you amazed by how
magnificent this diamond is?

468
00:23:28,780 --> 00:23:31,120
Sir, you must be joking.

469
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:33,300
Hey, come on, do it properly this time.

470
00:23:36,300 --> 00:23:38,960
What's wrong with you?
Pull yourself together, kettle!

471
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:41,600
Why?

472
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:42,860
Sir.

473
00:23:42,860 --> 00:23:46,560
That's right, there should be the
stone we turned into a diamond first.

474
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:47,740
This one, this one.

475
00:23:47,740 --> 00:23:48,620
What?

476
00:23:54,360 --> 00:23:56,840
Hey, kettle, hurry up and do something!

477
00:23:56,840 --> 00:23:59,000
Kettle.

478
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:02,660
You can't trust that kettle, you know.

479
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:20,460
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling

480
00:24:21,720 --> 00:24:27,080
walking while looking back,
led by the hand of Gaaja

481
00:24:27,940 --> 00:24:34,240
that strange feeling I had back then

482
00:24:34,940 --> 00:24:39,500
so on the tiles of the arcade street

483
00:24:39,500 --> 00:24:45,300
I tried walking only on the black ones

484
00:24:47,700 --> 00:24:51,440
Everyone was a child once

485
00:24:51,440 --> 00:24:53,560
but everyone has forgotten

486
00:24:54,480 --> 00:24:57,580
the politicians with
their self-important faces

487
00:24:57,580 --> 00:25:00,920
and that aunty who's a thorn in your side

488
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:03,860
come and take a turn

489
00:25:04,460 --> 00:25:06,580
that image

490
00:25:07,460 --> 00:25:11,660
you can meet everyone, everyone

491
00:25:12,220 --> 00:25:16,300
over there, it's Kameari

492
00:25:17,260 --> 00:25:19,600
surely it's Kameari

493
00:25:21,160 --> 00:25:24,860
everyone, come on over to our town

494
00:25:26,040 --> 00:25:26,440
Thank you

495
00:25:29,660 --> 00:25:32,220
The positive electrode falls
for Lemon at first sight.

496
00:25:32,220 --> 00:25:36,100
So you've finally awakened to
the feelings of a normal young man

497
00:25:36,100 --> 00:25:38,600
What? No reply to your email?

498
00:25:38,800 --> 00:25:39,940
No, no, that won't do.

499
00:25:39,940 --> 00:25:42,060
Feelings don't come across through email.

500
00:25:42,060 --> 00:25:44,400
A man should go straight at it and take his chances,
even if he gets shot down.

501
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:46,880
Next time: falling for Lemon at first sight.

502
00:25:46,880 --> 00:25:47,840
Take care.

503
00:25:51,720 --> 00:25:53,940
Well, there's sure to be a wall.

504
00:25:53,940 --> 00:25:59,120
Everyone, come on over to our town!

505
00:25:59,980 --> 00:26:00,740
Thank you.

